note: Acting on a whole group: "remove the tasks that are done", "set every task's done to yes".
a task has a name (text), a done (yes or no) and an age (a number).
a task is finished if its done is yes.
let tasks be a list of (a new task with name "a", done yes and age 3), (a new task with name "b", done no and age 9), (a new task with name "c", done yes and age 1), (a new task with name "d", done no and age 20).
let same be tasks.
remove the finished tasks.
say the number of items in tasks, the number of items in same.
remove the tasks whose age is over 10.
say tasks.
let scores be a list of 5, 60, 70, 2 and 99.
remove the scores that are below 10.
say scores.
remove the scores where it is above 90.
say scores.
let words be a list of "apple", "", "pear" and "".
remove the words that are empty.
say words.
let chores be a list of (a new task with name "x", done no and age 1), (a new task with name "y", done no and age 2).
set every chore's done to yes.
add 10 to every chore's age.
say chores.
if every chore is finished, say "All done.".
remove the finished chores.
say the number of items in chores.
